      },
      "worked": "\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=\\sqrt{x-1},\\quad x\\geq1\\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x-1}}\\quad(x>1)\\\\f'(x)&\\to+\\infty\\quad\\text{as }x\\to1^+\\end{align*}$$\n\n Since $f(1)=0$, $f$ has no vertical asymptote at $x=1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
